    "Yes. Gruffudd ap Llywelyn ruled the whole of Wales from 1055 to 1063, the only king ever to do so. Before him Rhodri Mawr and Hywel Dda ruled most of the country, and later the princes of Gwynedd were recognised as Princes of Wales.",
    "Do. Rheolodd Gruffudd ap Llywelyn Gymru gyfan o 1055 hyd 1063, yr unig frenin erioed i wneud hynny. Cyn hynny rheolodd Rhodri Mawr a Hywel Dda y rhan fwyaf o’r wlad, ac yn ddiweddarach cydnabuwyd tywysogion Gwynedd yn Dywysogion Cymru.",
