  Q("land-of-song", "Why is Wales called the land of song?", "Pam y gelwir Cymru’n wlad y gân?",
    "Gerald of Wales wrote in the 1190s that the Welsh sang in parts, not in unison, as no other people did. The chapels, the cymanfa ganu, the male voice choirs, the eisteddfodau and the rugby crowds have kept that tradition loud ever since.",
    "Ysgrifennodd Gerallt Gymro yn y 1190au fod y Cymry’n canu mewn rhannau, nid yn unsain, fel na wnâi’r un bobl arall. Mae’r capeli, y gymanfa ganu, y corau meibion, yr eisteddfodau a thorfeydd y rygbi wedi cadw’r traddodiad hwnnw’n uchel byth ers hynny.",
    ["person-gerallt-gymro.html", "trail-song.html", "symbols.html"]),
